@startuml
title D&D Simple - Dashboard Derived-State Flow

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
autonumber

actor User
participant "CharacterDashboardPage" as Page
participant "useCharacterBuilder" as Builder
participant "useCharacterDerivedState" as Hook
participant "fetchCharacterDerivedState" as Fetch
participant "charactersRouter" as Router
participant "requireAuth" as Auth
participant "character.controller" as Controller
participant "character-effects.service" as Effects
database "PostgreSQL via Prisma" as DB
participant "CharacterSheet" as Sheet

User -> Page: Edit dashboard build/resource state
Page -> Builder: Apply local builder mutation
Builder --> Page: builderState, selected refs, previewCharacter
Page -> Page: Build feature-choice selections
Page -> Page: Build builderActionPreview
Page -> Hook: characterId + preview payload
Hook -> Fetch: fetchCharacterDerivedState(id, preview, token)

alt Body-only overrides exist
  Fetch -> Router: POST /characters/:id/derived
else Query-only overrides
  Fetch -> Router: GET /characters/:id/derived
end

Router -> Auth: require bearer token
Auth --> Router: authenticated user
Router -> Controller: derived-state handler
Controller -> Controller: Validate id and preview input
Controller -> Controller: Normalize override payload
Controller -> Effects: findCharacterDerivedStateForUser(userId, id, overrides)
Effects -> DB: Read owned character and persisted state
Effects -> DB: Read reference rows and rule documents
Effects -> Effects: Resolve effective class/species/background/level
Effects -> Effects: Merge persisted and preview feature choices
Effects -> Effects: Build active sources
Effects -> Effects: Derive stats, actions, defenses, resources, spells
Effects --> Controller: CharacterDerivedState
Controller --> Fetch: JSON response
Fetch --> Hook: CharacterDerivedState
Hook --> Page: derivedState React state
Page -> Sheet: Render derived dashboard data

@enduml
